{
  "fixture": "landmines",
  "description": "The adversarial set: every edge case, ambiguity, and interaction the v0.7.0 spec had to settle, each with its EXACT declared outcome — which problem/advisory fires at what severity and location, or that the case builds clean. Cases that cannot live in git (case-only twins, symlinks, nested .git, --clean containment) are generated at runtime by runtime-cases.mjs and share this expectation schema.",
  "harnessContract": {
    "run": "per case: unify build -s <case>/src -o <tmp>/dist <flags>, wrapped in a hard 30s timeout — the v0.6 engine hung forever on a missing <include>; a hang is a failure, never a wait.",
    "diagnostics": "stderr parsed via the stable `FILE:LINE: SEVERITY: ` prefix (line optional). Declared lists are exhaustive when diagnosticsExhaustive=true: one undeclared diagnostic of either severity fails the case. This is the mechanical enforcement of the closed problem/advisory catalogue (conformance spec §14.2/§14.3) and of the content-loss law's flip side — nothing may fire that the spec does not name.",
    "trees": "when expectedTree is set, comparison is byte-exact and bidirectional. expectFiles/expectAbsent assert presence/absence relative to the output dir. expectContains maps output files to required substrings; expectNotContains to forbidden ones.",
    "publish": "published=false cases pre-seed the output dir with a sentinel tree and assert it byte-untouched after the run (PUB-01), and assert exit matches.",
    "severityTokens": "the parser accepts only 'problem' and 'advisory' as severity tokens; any 'warning'/'error:' line fails the case (DIA-01)."
  },
  "harnessRules": [
    "DIA-01",
    "DIA-05",
    "DIA-06",
    "MRG-18"
  ],
  "cases": {
